.TH QBIBLE 1 "October 2026" "qbible 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qbible \- a modern, ad-free Bible reader (King James Version)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qbible
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qbible
reads, searches and navigates the King James Version of the Bible from the
terminal or, with \fBqbible serve\fR, in a web browser on the same computer.
It works offline, contains no adverts and does not track its users.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "read " REFERENCE
Show a verse, range, chapter or book, e.g. \fBqbible read John 3:16\fR,
\fBqbible read Psalm 23\fR, \fBqbible read 1 Cor 13:4\-7\fR.
.TP
.BI "chapter " "BOOK CHAPTER"
Show a whole chapter.
.TP
.BR next ", " previous " [\fB\-\-from\fR \fIREFERENCE\fR]"
Read the chapter after or before the last passage you read (the saved reading position).
.TP
.BR random " [\fB\-\-testament\fR OT|NT]"
Show a random verse.
.TP
.B books
List the books of the Bible with their chapter counts and abbreviations.
.TP
.BI "search " WORDS
Search. A quoted argument is an exact phrase (\fBqbible search "fear not"\fR);
separate words must all appear. Options: \fB\-\-limit\fR N, \fB\-\-page\fR N,
\fB\-\-context\fR [N], \fB\-\-phrase\fR, \fB\-\-words\fR, \fB\-\-any\fR,
\fB\-\-sort\fR canonical|relevance, \fB\-\-book\fR BOOK, \fB\-\-testament\fR OT|NT, \fB\-\-count\fR.
.TP
.BI "ref " REFERENCE
Check and normalise a reference.
.TP
.BR bookmark " add|list|open|label|remove ..."
Manage bookmarks, e.g. \fBqbible bookmark add John 3:16 \-\-label "God's love"\fR.
.TP
.BR history " [list|clear]"
Show or clear the reading history.
.TP
.B shell
Interactive reading mode (type \fBhelp\fR inside it).
.TP
.BR serve " [\fB\-\-port\fR N] [\fB\-\-open\fR]"
Start the browser interface on http://127.0.0.1:8737/ (local only).
.TP
.BR translations ", " import ", " remove\-translation ", " validate
Manage and check translations.
.TP
.BR config " [list|get|set|unset]"
Show or change settings.
.TP
.BR paths ", " completion
Show file locations; print the bash completion script.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-translation " \fIID\fR"
Translation to use (default \fBkjv\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-colour " auto|always|never, " \-\-plain
Control colour. Colour is only used on terminals; \fBNO_COLOR\fR is respected.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 nothing found; 2 usage error; 3 invalid reference or unknown bookmark;
4 data or configuration problem; 130 interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/qbible/translations/kjv.sqlite
The bundled King James Version (read-only).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/qbible/user.sqlite
Your bookmarks and reading history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/qbible/translations/
Translations you have imported.
.TP
.I ~/.config/qbible/config.ini
Settings (\fBqbible config\fR).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\fBQBIBLE_DATA_HOME\fR, \fBQBIBLE_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBQBIBLE_TRANSLATIONS_PATH\fR,
\fBQBIBLE_SHARE_DIR\fR, \fBQBIBLE_WEB_DIR\fR override file locations;
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR and \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR are honoured; \fBNO_COLOR\fR disables colour.
